<pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I52b5052942f4590e7c722d7323ed793a563603f6" commit="8946eb0fdb51fd86a2b0c51a55c867e91eb1a689" commit_message="UPSTREAM: ipip: Properly mark ipip GRO packets as encapsulated.  ipip encapsulated packets can be merged together by GRO but the result does not have the proper GSO type set or even marked as being encapsulated at all. Later retransmission of these packets will likely fail if the device does not support ipip offloads. This is similar to the issue resolved in IPv6 sit in feec0cb3 (&quot;ipv6: gro: support sit protocol&quot;).  Reported-by: Patrick Boutilier &lt;boutilpj@ednet.ns.ca&gt; Fixes: 9667e9bb (&quot;ipip: Add gro callbacks to ipip offload&quot;) Tested-by: Patrick Boutilier &lt;boutilpj@ednet.ns.ca&gt; Acked-by: Eric Dumazet &lt;edumazet@google.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Jesse Gross &lt;jesse@kernel.org&gt; Signed-off-by: David S. Miller &lt;davem@davemloft.net&gt;  (cherry picked from commit b8cba75bdf6a48ea4811bbefb11a94a5c7281b68)  BUG=b:32515955, chromium:672642 TEST=Compile kernel and run trybots.  Change-Id: I52b5052942f4590e7c722d7323ed793a563603f6 Signed-off-by: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/419340 Reviewed-by: Mattias Nissler &lt;mnissler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="419340" owner_email="benchan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/40/419340/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I33a0cd7d9fadd1b85086ded6eff0544846fe3180" commit="27a0244dde1e063296c5bef802e1624d31e35a30" commit_message="BACKPORT: tunnels: Don't apply GRO to multiple layers of encapsulation.  When drivers express support for TSO of encapsulated packets, they only mean that they can do it for one layer of encapsulation. Supporting additional levels would mean updating, at a minimum, more IP length fields and they are unaware of this.  No encapsulation device expresses support for handling offloaded encapsulated packets, so we won't generate these types of frames in the transmit path. However, GRO doesn't have a check for multiple levels of encapsulation and will attempt to build them.  UDP tunnel GRO actually does prevent this situation but it only handles multiple UDP tunnels stacked on top of each other. This generalizes that solution to prevent any kind of tunnel stacking that would cause problems.  Fixes: bf5a755f (&quot;net-gre-gro: Add GRE support to the GRO stack&quot;) Signed-off-by: Jesse Gross &lt;jesse@kernel.org&gt; Signed-off-by: David S. Miller &lt;davem@davemloft.net&gt;  (cherry picked from commit fac8e0f579695a3ecbc4d3cac369139d7f819971)  BUG=b:32515955, chromium:672642 TEST=Trybot runs on paladin and release builders.  Change-Id: I33a0cd7d9fadd1b85086ded6eff0544846fe3180 Signed-off-by: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/419341 Reviewed-by: Mattias Nissler &lt;mnissler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="419341" owner_email="benchan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/41/419341/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ica125ce3a3d30633c3b74c37676b966bdbc4b47b" commit="e265bcee5165ce84c4be7180fbd63cc967a57f4e" commit_message="BACKPORT: net: add recursion limit to GRO  Currently, GRO can do unlimited recursion through the gro_receive handlers.  This was fixed for tunneling protocols by limiting tunnel GRO to one level with encap_mark, but both VLAN and TEB still have this problem.  Thus, the kernel is vulnerable to a stack overflow, if we receive a packet composed entirely of VLAN headers.  This patch adds a recursion counter to the GRO layer to prevent stack overflow.  When a gro_receive function hits the recursion limit, GRO is aborted for this skb and it is processed normally.  This recursion counter is put in the GRO CB, but could be turned into a percpu counter if we run out of space in the CB.  Thanks to Vladimr Bene &lt;vbenes@redhat.com&gt; for the initial bug report.  Fixes: CVE-2016-7039 Fixes: 9b174d88c257 (&quot;net: Add Transparent Ethernet Bridging GRO support.&quot;) Fixes: 66e5133f19e9 (&quot;vlan: Add GRO support for non hardware accelerated vlan&quot;) Signed-off-by: Sabrina Dubroca &lt;sd@queasysnail.net&gt; Reviewed-by: Jiri Benc &lt;jbenc@redhat.com&gt; Acked-by: Hannes Frederic Sowa &lt;hannes@stressinduktion.org&gt; Acked-by: Tom Herbert &lt;tom@herbertland.com&gt; Signed-off-by: David S. Miller &lt;davem@davemloft.net&gt;  (cherry picked from commit fcd91dd449867c6bfe56a81cabba76b829fd05cd)  Notes on backport: ------------------------------------------------------------------------ The upstream patch doesn't apply cleanly on top of ChromeOS 3.18 kernel.  - The call_gro_receive change doesn't apply to the following files   as no call to .gro_receive exists in the code yet.       drivers/net/geneve.c      net/8021q/vlan.c      net/ethernet/eth.c  - call_gro_receive is used instead of call_gro_receive_sk in   net/ipv4/udp_offload.c as the .gro_receive callback doesn't take   `struct sk` argument. ------------------------------------------------------------------------  BUG=b:32515955, chromium:672642 TEST=Trybot runs on paladin and release builders.  Change-Id: Ica125ce3a3d30633c3b74c37676b966bdbc4b47b Signed-off-by: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/419721 Reviewed-by: Mattias Nissler &lt;mnissler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="419721" owner_email="benchan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/21/419721/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I18836f034c0fdc0bb6a850b82bb8a7eb920a6051" commit="9ef9b8396c464285a1e31240514da35a347ceefb" commit_message="platform_CUPSDaemon: Added systemd support.  BUG=chromium:583671 TEST=test_that [ip] platform_CUPSDaemon. CQ-DEPEND=CL:408138  Change-Id: I18836f034c0fdc0bb6a850b82bb8a7eb920a6051 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/411301 Commit-Ready: Sabin Floares &lt;sabin.floares@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Sabin Floares &lt;sabin.floares@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="411301" owner_email="sabin.floares@gmail.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/01/411301/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id2e6565b28ecff2b43a3e7a3ccab20779d3ac64d" commit="54e1ff694834dff79aff8c41d4d081e26a3de43b" commit_message="chromeos-base/autotest-tests: Remove mandatory flag.  BUG=chromium:583671 TEST=Built packages. CQ-DEPEND=CL:411301  Change-Id: Id2e6565b28ecff2b43a3e7a3ccab20779d3ac64d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/408138 Commit-Ready: Sabin Floares &lt;sabin.floares@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Sabin Floares &lt;sabin.floares@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="408138" owner_email="sabin.floares@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/38/408138/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I1cd1d5fc3fa5bdffdd24a10cfeab90d6cc5d5444" commit="e0a0f7574a2b72d2dd01eeca1b037599c8951891" commit_message="Test for suspend-resume timing check  BUG=chromium:653315 TEST=locally tested  Change-Id: I1cd1d5fc3fa5bdffdd24a10cfeab90d6cc5d5444 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/418712 Commit-Ready: Kalin Stoyanov &lt;kalin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kalin Stoyanov &lt;kalin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ruchi Jahagirdar &lt;rjahagir@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="418712" owner_email="kalin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/12/418712/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ifb5e65a795cd255d18357850f7b402a4d83cdd32" commit="06db9a34a0fe9870baf377b572c925518e24bfa2" commit_message="Adding suspend tests to HDMI test  - suspend - suspend and resume before testing HDMI audio - suspend_while_playback - play audio, suspend and resume, stop audio before testing HDMI audio  BUG=chromium:651603 TEST=tested DUTs in lab  Change-Id: Ifb5e65a795cd255d18357850f7b402a4d83cdd32 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/415115 Commit-Ready: Kalin Stoyanov &lt;kalin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kalin Stoyanov &lt;kalin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ruchi Jahagirdar &lt;rjahagir@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="415115" owner_email="kalin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/15/415115/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I5d296657da7c6561da86266724692f9659c15163" commit="01d1c5b05ee0f4114614514cbcf797fb90ad1751" commit_message="security_ASLR: Make finding processes more robust  There have been a few flaky runs where the first line of `pidof ${name}` is not the process we were looking for and goes away before we are able to look for /proc/${pid}/maps. This change removes the code path where we only look at `pidof` and instead always requires that the parent process is specified to reduce flake.  BUG=chromium:618382 TEST=test_that cyan security_ASLR TEST=test_that lakitu security_ASLR  Change-Id: I5d296657da7c6561da86266724692f9659c15163 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/419096 Commit-Ready: Luis Hector Chavez &lt;lhchavez@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Luis Hector Chavez &lt;lhchavez@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Jorge Lucangeli Obes &lt;jorgelo@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Daniel Wang &lt;wonderfly@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Andrey Ulanov &lt;andreyu@google.com&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="419096" owner_email="lhchavez@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/96/419096/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Icbd22f04dd434ad1e1fe8ae42a2385232b419be0" commit="423d6d8ff1af9ada36fe0090596cf8804c5b02c2" commit_message="init: halt service if initial check fails  If the pre-startup phase fails, then there's a problem with the watchdog. Stop upstart from trying to respawn us all the time in that case.  This fixes the restart storm/spam seen when we build images for real devices, but then boot them in a VM where there is no watchdog service.  BUG=chromium:667075 TEST=startup still works on a real device TEST=startup halts in a VM  Change-Id: Icbd22f04dd434ad1e1fe8ae42a2385232b419be0 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/419215 Commit-Ready: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mattias Nissler &lt;mnissler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="419215" owner_email="vapier@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/daisydog" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/daisydog" ref="refs/changes/15/419215/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I493569a9e62dd7ef6f6c4809948c5ec6950a1884" commit="554c800b73eba775424e0c8a3e5855fc3b087497" commit_message="metrics: register new Watchdog.StartupFailed enum  This is used whenever the watchdog service (daisydog) fails to start up correctly.  We don't expect this to happen on real devices, so we want to get a handle if it actually does (and how often).  Chrome CL: https://codereview.chromium.org/2571873002  BUG=chromium:673501 TEST=`metrics_client -v Watchdog.StartupFailed` now works  Change-Id: I493569a9e62dd7ef6f6c4809948c5ec6950a1884 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/418836 Commit-Ready: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mattias Nissler &lt;mnissler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="418836" owner_email="vapier@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/36/418836/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="9086.0.0-rc2"/></manifest>